---
// How aws-platform-terraform is built and drilled, drawn from its README and live-drill workflow.
---

<svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 800 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="aws-diagram-title aws-diagram-desc">
  <title id="aws-diagram-title">How aws-platform-terraform is built and drilled</title>
  <desc id="aws-diagram-desc">
    A scheduled Claude Code run builds the next roadmap item and pushes to main. CI runs offline:
    format, validate, tflint, checkov and terraform test with mock providers and Moto. If it passes,
    a live drill in GitHub Actions signs in to a real AWS account through OIDC with no stored keys.
    In the account it applies the stack, records evidence, destroys it and checks nothing is left.
    A drill report is committed to docs/live. Rodrigo reviews the work and the learning note.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="aws-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path class="arrowhead" d="M0 0 8 4 0 8z"></path>
    </marker>
  </defs>

